Answer: The dot operator is used to access the contents of an object through its reference variable. Example:

```java
s1.id = 1;
s1.name = "Sahana";
s1.eat();
```

s1. goes inside the object and accesses the required property or behaviour.

Answer: Values are assigned using the object reference and the dot operator.

```java
s1.id = 1;
s1.name = "Sahana";
s1.marks = 55;
s2.id = 2;
s2.name = "Omkar";
s2.marks = 99;
```

The properties of the first object are accessed using s1. The properties of the second object are accessed using s2.

